<!--Post: 5288--><!--Time: 1107027307-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5288"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 29, 2005 - 11:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have come to suspect one of his names it Thomas... <BR> <BR>When looking at his communications in total that we know of, the Thomas B. King one stands out to me like he may have gone to far...it doesn&#39;t quite fit with the others; it doesn&#39;t include &#34;kill&#34;...Thomas is used twice...Thomas B. King = Thomas is king?... <BR> <BR>Bill Thomas Killman <BR>Thomas B. King <BR>S. Killett <BR> <BR>I have never put much stock in BTK meaning anything other than bind torture, kill...however, I do remember when we were kids forming clubs, and even grown-ups do it to form companies, using our intials to come up with a club, company, or brand name.  One possible theory: Kevin Bright &amp; Thomas, with Thomas being the person we know as BTK.  Thomas uses this as a constant threat to Kevin Bright of his complicity in the 1974 crimes.  <BR> <BR>And why &#34;S.&#34; in S. Killett and not something that = BTK?  No &#34;B&#34;?  No capital &#34;T&#34;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5288-->
<!--Post: 5380--><!--Time: 1107096464-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5380"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 6:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I believe his name is roger. Why I can&#39;t say meaning I don&#39;t know the reason. I think that LE believes his name might be roger. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5380-->
<!--Post: 5383--><!--Time: 1107098828-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5383"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 7:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Scbenson <BR> <BR>Maybe you belive that because of the arrest of  Roger Valadez? <BR> <BR>maybe we should keep in mind that ROGER also is part of the sentence  <BR> <BR>ROGER OVER!&#40;meaning &#34;OK message recived&#34; in radio communication&#41; <BR> <BR>Maybe BTK signed one of his letters ROGER and therefor the police think his name is Roger but in fact he ment ROGER OVER!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5383-->
<!--Post: 5386--><!--Time: 1107099857-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5386"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 7:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->No love for Thomas?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5386-->
<!--Post: 5405--><!--Time: 1107109762-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5405"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 10:29 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Your right I do believe it because of that mans arrest. I have always had the suspicion that other then the tip they recieved this man fit something they thought about BTK. I dont know what that is but I think the roger may be it. As far as your sign off theory, I don&#39;t see it but anythings possible and its just as plausible as my &#34;name&#34; theory.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5405-->
<!--Post: 5429--><!--Time: 1107117646-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5429"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 12:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thomas as a first, middle or last name, YES! I think BTK&#39;s name, if he can be caught, will turn out to be a more familiar-sounding appellation. First name of Tom, last name of Thomas, middle name Thomas; commonly seen enough to placate BTK&#39;s concerns, yet daring enough to dangle as a clue. I&#39;m a believer.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5429-->
<!--Post: 5458--><!--Time: 1107136195-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5458"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 5:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wouldn&#39;t be surprised to find his name is something obtuse, like Buford, or Alois.  I really don&#39;t put a lot of stock in his correspondence, but, who knows...?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5458-->
<!--Post: 5462--><!--Time: 1107138084-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5462"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 6:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Roger that. Pilot lingo. What about Allen or Richard? Popular names years ago. I&#39;ll be disappointed if he has some dork name. Perhaps it is time for the Ouiji Board.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5462-->
<!--Post: 5496--><!--Time: 1107148605-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5496"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 9:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I still like Thomas &#40;or Tom&#41; because BTK taunts and takes the occasional risk. A little touch like this one seems up his alley. But his real name could easily end up being Gatewood Leathers or some such thing. &#40;There actually was a Gatewood Leathers, connected with the Civil War in some capacity. I remember my father mentioning that name.&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5496-->
<!--Post: 5505--><!--Time: 1107150004-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5505"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 9:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tomas????<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5505-->
<!--Post: 5512--><!--Time: 1107151953-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5512"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 30, 2005 - 10:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><i>If</i> BTK&#39;s initials reveal anything about his name, I can see the &#34;T&#34; for Tom possibly being accurate. Even after killing several, Bundy would still say &#34;Just call me Ted.&#34; BTK seems cocky enough to have used Tom. Or Ted. Or Troy. Or Terrance. In the context of if initials mean anything as to his name, something about &#34;Thomas&#34; slightly gripped me.  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5512-->
<!--Post: 5593--><!--Time: 1107211728-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5593"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Affie4u<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Affie4u<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 31, 2005 - 2:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Since, we are on this subject, I could be wrong, but what if is name is Bill? Or william?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5593-->
<!--Post: 9211--><!--Time: 1109432556-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9211"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 7:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I guess not!!! LOL<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9211-->
<!--Post: 10287--><!--Time: 1109875421-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10287"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 10:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There is a Thomas Rader who lives in North St., between Woodland and Webb, just one block off 13th. I wonder if Dennis and he are related. This Thomas lives right in the middle of where all the murders occurred. <BR> <BR>Some people wonder about how it was possible for Dennis Rader to dump Marine Hedge&#39;s car eight miles from where he lives, and then make it back to his home.  <BR> <BR>Some people say he must&#39;ve taken a bus, train, or asked a friend or family for a ride&#40;or church member&#41;.  <BR> <BR>How about if he dropped-in one of his relatives&#39; home in Wichita, then asked for a ride to his home? <BR> <BR>How many hot-shot murderers do you know of, who got to their victims homes by walking?  <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10287-->
</table></td></tr></table>
